        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): catch unhandled rejections in webhook and ingress worker shutdown",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Telegram webhook shutdown could leave owned resources active when an early teardown step failed: a synchronous `server.close()` throw, a `bot.stop()` rejection, or a transport-close rejection could skip later cleanup (bot stop, undici transport close, webhook status, diagnostic heartbeat). Ingress-worker `stop()` could also race on repeated calls and leave `worker.terminate()` rejections unobserved.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nIndependently guard each ordered webhook shutdown phase via `runTelegramWebhookShutdownPhases` so one sync/async failure cannot skip later owned cleanup, and wrap the path so fire-and-forget abort listeners never leak unhandled rejections. Startup failure cleanup uses `.catch(() => undefined)` so cleanup noise cannot mask the original startup error. Ingress-worker `stop()` shares one in-flight promise and observes terminate rejections.\n\nNon-goals: no UI drive-by edits; no committed `proof-*.mts` script (proof cases live in vitest against the production helper).\n\nCollision check: searched open PRs for `runTelegramWebhookShutdownPhases`, webhook shutdown skip, ingress-worker terminate rejection; no stronger same-fix open competitor.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators restarting or aborting a Telegram webhook account no longer risk leaked transports, stale webhook connected status, or leftover diagnostic heartbeats when one shutdown step fails. Process logs no longer see unhandled rejections from webhook/ingress shutdown paths.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact head: `aac474a46e7803ea688ba9f398c70240b86a7555`\n- Rebased onto current `origin/main`.\n- Surface: 6 `extensions/telegram/` files only (UI drive-bys and committed proof script removed).\n\nFocused tests at this head:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/telegram/src/webhook-shutdown.proof.test.ts extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.test.ts -- --run --reporter=verbose\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/telegram/src/webhook.test.ts -- --run -t \"does not leak unhandled|does not skip\"\n```\n\n```\n ✓ negative control: sync server.close throw skips later cleanup\n ✓ positive control: guarded phases continue after sync close throw\n ✓ valid path: clean close runs full ordered teardown\n ✓ createTelegramIngressWorker stop > is idempotent and returns the same promise on repeated calls\n ✓ createTelegramIngressWorker stop > routes forced terminate rejections during stop timeout\n ✓ createTelegramIngressWorker stop > does not leak unhandled rejections when terminate rejects\n ✓ webhook tests matching does not leak unhandled|does not skip — 3 passed\n\n[case 1] negative control closeServer=1 stopBot=0 closeTransport=0 noteStop=0 stopDiagnostics=0 errors=1\n[case 2] positive control stopBot=1 closeTransport=1 noteStop=1 stopDiagnostics=1 errors=[\"webhook server close failed: server close failed\"]\n[case 3] valid path phases_ok=true errors=0\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n### Behavior addressed\n\nSync `server.close()` throw must not skip bot/transport/status/diagnostics cleanup; ingress-worker repeated `stop()` must share one promise and observe terminate rejections.\n\n### Environment\n\n- OS: Linux x86_64\n- Node: v22.22.0\n- head: aac474a46e7803ea688ba9f398c70240b86a7555\n\n### Exact commands run\n\nSame focused vitest commands above (production `runTelegramWebhookShutdownPhases` + ingress-worker stop path).\n\n### Observed output after fix\n\nSee Evidence diagnostics: negative control skips later phases; positive control continues all later phases after sync close throw and does not reject; valid path runs every phase once with zero errors.\n\n### What was not tested\n\n- Live configured Telegram Bot API webhook gateway abort/restart with a real bot token (local OpenClaw install currently has no `channels.telegram` config). Cleanup contract is covered via the production phase helper and webhook/ingress unit paths.\n\n## Risk / Compatibility\n\nMedium-low (`merge-risk: availability` remains relevant for teardown sequencing). Behavior is fail-soft: phase failures are logged and later owned cleanup still runs. No config keys, no SDK surface changes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [co-mind](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
        "branch": "fix/channel-bugs-batch-2026-07-06",
